From 3e4303a78b29f006c5264dd71a94e7e079781ecf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:13:00 -0400
Subject: Derive the compositor-wide DPMS flag from monitor state; remember
 per-output DPMS-off across reconnects

Bug: g_pCompositor->m_dpmsStateOn is what misc:mouse_move_enables_dpms and
misc:key_press_enables_dpms consult: while it is false, any pointer or keyboard event
runs dpms(TOGGLE_ACTION_ENABLE, nullopt) and lights every monitor. The dpms dispatcher
(src/config/shared/actions/ConfigActions.cpp, Actions::dpms) assigned that flag from the
last monitor it touched, even with a monitor filter, so `dpms off <one monitor>` set the
compositor-wide flag to false while the other monitors stayed lit. The next mouse move on
any lit monitor then switched the blanked one back on. The wlr-output-power-management
path (src/protocols/OutputPower.cpp -> CMonitor::setDPMS) never updated the flag at all,
so a client blanking every monitor through that protocol left the flag true and input did
not wake them.

Evidence (2026-09-17 23:02, three-monitor amdgpu desktop, Hyprland 0.56.2): an idle
per-monitor blank of HDMI-A-1 via `hl.dsp.dpms({ action = "off", monitor = "HDMI-A-1" })`
went dark on time and came back on as soon as the pointer moved on DP-1, with no input
on HDMI-A-1, no hypridle Resumed, and no dpms-on dispatch from any client.

Fix:
- CMonitor::setDPMS() recomputes g_pCompositor->m_dpmsStateOn from every enabled
  monitor: false only when all of them are DPMS-off. CMonitor::onDisconnect() recomputes
  it too, so losing the last lit monitor is reflected. Actions::dpms() no longer assigns
  the flag. Every DPMS path (dispatcher, wlr-output-power, the input-driven enable)
  now agrees. With all monitors off, input still turns everything on as before; with
  only some monitors off, input on a lit monitor no longer touches the dark ones.
- A file-local set in src/output/Monitor.cpp remembers, by output name, monitors that
  were switched off, and CMonitor::onConnect() brings a returning output up dark if its
  name is in it, in addition to the compositor-wide inheritance already there. Without
  this, correcting the flag would have re-lit any panel that drops HPD after losing
  signal and reconnects a second later (input auto-scan) after every per-monitor blank,
  including a cold link training on DisplayPort. An unfiltered `dpms on` (which is what
  the input-driven enable issues) clears the whole set, so an output that was unplugged
  while off and comes back after a compositor-wide wake is lit; a per-monitor `dpms on`
  clears only that name.

No class layout changes (file-local static, one free function in namespace Monitor), so
plugins built against the unpatched headers keep working.

Upstream: same code on main as of 2026-09-17 (Actions::dpms assigns the flag per
monitor; OutputPower never does). Not filed (hyprwm AI-usage policy; see the registry).

Retires when: an Arch hyprland release whose dpms dispatcher does not mark the compositor
DPMS-off after a filtered `dpms off`, i.e. moving the mouse on a lit monitor does not wake a
monitor blanked individually. Packaged locally as 0.56.2-3.3 together with
hyprland-dpms-off-on-connect.patch and hyprland-idle-inhibit-unchanged-noop.patch; any
Arch pkgrel or pkgver bump outranks it automatically (the pacman hook then says whether
to rebase or retire).

diff -ruN a/src/output/Monitor.cpp b/src/output/Monitor.cpp

(Patch carried in ~/pkgs by Fred's Omarchy workstation; registry: https://github.com/greenermoose/omarchy-fred-ecosystem)

